IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `au-part5-readings`

-- Tests for the rules of reading in Part 5 (ss 12, 15A, 15AA, 15AB(2)(3), 15AC, 15AD, 15B(3)(3A)(4)(b), 16 to 18A, 18B(4)-(6),
-- 20, 21, 23). Expected values are written from the text. A gate that does not open returns NOTHING, and is asserted.

§ `Section 12`

-- "Every section of an Act shall have effect as a substantive enactment without introductory words."
#ASSERT `has effect as a substantive enactment without introductory words` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not a section of an Act: the section says nothing.
#ASSERT `has effect as a substantive enactment without introductory words` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 15A`

-- An enactment that would not have been construed as exceeding the power is read subject to the Constitution and is valid.
#ASSERT `section 15A treats the enactment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `read and construed subject to the Constitution, and valid`
-- One that would have been construed as in excess is nevertheless valid to the extent to which it is not in excess.
#ASSERT `section 15A treats the enactment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `valid to the extent to which it is not in excess of the legislative power of the Commonwealth`
-- Not an enactment of an Act (for example an instrument): s 15A does not speak of it.
#ASSERT `section 15A treats the enactment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `section 15A treats the enactment` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 15AA`

`candidate one` MEANS `A candidate interpretation` OF "the first reading", TRUE, TRUE
`candidate two` MEANS `A candidate interpretation` OF "the second reading", FALSE, TRUE
`candidate three` MEANS `A candidate interpretation` OF "the third reading", TRUE, FALSE
`candidate four` MEANS `A candidate interpretation` OF "the fourth reading", FALSE, FALSE
`candidate one with the purpose unstated` MEANS `A candidate interpretation` OF "the first reading", TRUE, FALSE

-- Exactly one reading best achieves the purpose or object: it is the one preferred over each other.
#ASSERT `the interpretation to be preferred` (LIST `candidate one`, `candidate two`) EQUALS JUST `candidate one`
#ASSERT `the interpretation to be preferred` (LIST `candidate two`, `candidate three`) EQUALS JUST `candidate three`
-- "whether or not that purpose or object is expressly stated in the Act": the answer is the same.
#ASSERT `the interpretation to be preferred` (LIST `candidate one with the purpose unstated`, `candidate four`) EQUALS JUST `candidate one with the purpose unstated`
-- Two readings that both best achieve it: the section prefers "the" best reading and does not choose between equals (fork F20).
#ASSERT `the interpretation to be preferred` (LIST `candidate one`, `candidate three`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- None does: nothing is preferred.
#ASSERT `the interpretation to be preferred` (LIST `candidate two`, `candidate four`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the interpretation to be preferred` EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 15AB(2) and (3)`

-- (a) matters set out in the document as printed by the Government Printer: listed whatever the date.
#ASSERT `section 15AB(2) lists` `matters set out in the document containing the text of the Act as printed by the Government Printer` TRUE
#ASSERT `section 15AB(2) lists` `matters set out in the document containing the text of the Act as printed by the Government Printer` FALSE
-- (b) a report of a Royal Commission etc. "laid before either House ... before the time when the provision was enacted".
#ASSERT `section 15AB(2) lists` `a relevant report of a Royal Commission, Law Reform Commission, committee of inquiry or other similar body` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`section 15AB(2) lists` `a relevant report of a Royal Commission, Law Reform Commission, committee of inquiry or other similar body` FALSE)
-- (c) a report of a committee of the Parliament made before the provision was enacted.
#ASSERT `section 15AB(2) lists` `a relevant report of a committee of the Parliament or of either House` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`section 15AB(2) lists` `a relevant report of a committee of the Parliament or of either House` FALSE)
-- (d) a treaty referred to in the Act.
#ASSERT `section 15AB(2) lists` `a treaty or other international agreement that is referred to in the Act` FALSE
-- (e) an explanatory memorandum laid before or furnished to the members before the provision was enacted.
#ASSERT `section 15AB(2) lists` `an explanatory memorandum relating to the Bill, or any other relevant document, laid before or furnished to the members of either House by a Minister` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`section 15AB(2) lists` `an explanatory memorandum relating to the Bill, or any other relevant document, laid before or furnished to the members of either House by a Minister` FALSE)
-- (f) the second reading speech; (g) a document the Act declares relevant; (h) the Journals, Votes and Proceedings, debates.
#ASSERT `section 15AB(2) lists` `the Minister's second reading speech on the Bill containing the provision` FALSE
#ASSERT `section 15AB(2) lists` `a document declared by the Act to be a relevant document for the purposes of section 15AB` FALSE
#ASSERT `section 15AB(2) lists` `relevant material in the Journals of the Senate, the Votes and Proceedings of the House of Representatives or an official record of debates` FALSE
-- The list is not exhaustive, but other material is not "listed".
#ASSERT NOT (`section 15AB(2) lists` `other material` TRUE)
-- Listed material is considered only "in accordance with" subsection (1): capable of assisting and one of the three purposes.
#ASSERT `listed material may be considered under section 15AB(1)` `a treaty or other international agreement that is referred to in the Act` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `listed material may be considered under section 15AB(1)` `a treaty or other international agreement that is referred to in the Act` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`listed material may be considered under section 15AB(1)` `a treaty or other international agreement that is referred to in the Act` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`listed material may be considered under section 15AB(1)` `a treaty or other international agreement that is referred to in the Act` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`listed material may be considered under section 15AB(1)` `other material` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`listed material may be considered under section 15AB(1)` `a relevant report of a committee of the Parliament or of either House` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- (3): regard shall be had to both listed matters, and to any other relevant matter.
#ASSERT `regard must be had to` `the desirability of persons being able to rely on the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text of the provision taking into account its context in the Act and the purpose or object underlying the Act`
#ASSERT `regard must be had to` `the need to avoid prolonging legal or other proceedings without compensating advantage`
#ASSERT `regard must be had to` `any other relevant matter`
#ASSERT NOT (`regard must be had to` `a matter that is not relevant`)

§ `Section 15AC`

-- Same idea in a clearer style: the ideas are not taken to be different merely because the words differ.
#ASSERT `the ideas are taken to be different merely because different forms of words were used` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Without the earlier Act's idea, or without the clearer-style purpose, the section does not speak.
#ASSERT `the ideas are taken to be different merely because different forms of words were used` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the ideas are taken to be different merely because different forms of words were used` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the ideas are taken to be different merely because different forms of words were used` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 15AD`

#ASSERT `the example is exhaustive` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the example may extend the operation of the provision` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No example in the Act: nothing is said.
#ASSERT `the example is exhaustive` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the example may extend the operation of the provision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 15B(3), (3A) and (4)(b)`

#ASSERT `an Act in force in an external Territory is taken to have effect in its coastal sea as if it were part of the Territory` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`an Act in force in an external Territory is taken to have effect in its coastal sea as if it were part of the Territory` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`an Act in force in an external Territory is taken to have effect in its coastal sea as if it were part of the Territory` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the reference to the external Territories is taken to include the coastal sea` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the reference to the external Territories is taken to include the coastal sea` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the reference to the external Territories is taken to include the coastal sea` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `is in the coastal sea of an external Territory` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `is in the coastal sea of an external Territory` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`is in the coastal sea of an external Territory` FALSE FALSE)

§ `Section 16`

#ASSERT `a reference in an Act is construed as a reference to` `a reference to the Sovereign reigning at the time of the passing of the Act` EQUALS JUST `the Sovereign for the time being`
#ASSERT `a reference in an Act is construed as a reference to` `a reference to the Crown` EQUALS JUST `the Sovereign for the time being`
#ASSERT `a reference in an Act is construed as a reference to` `a reference to anyone else` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 16A`

#ASSERT `a reference to the Governor-General is deemed to include` `the Governor-General` FALSE
#ASSERT `a reference to the Governor-General is deemed to include` `the person for the time being administering the Government of the Commonwealth` FALSE
-- (b): a deputy is included only where the reference is in a provision conferring a power or function assigned to the deputy.
#ASSERT `a reference to the Governor-General is deemed to include` `a person to whom the Governor-General or the administrator has for the time being assigned a power or function as deputy` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a reference to the Governor-General is deemed to include` `a person to whom the Governor-General or the administrator has for the time being assigned a power or function as deputy` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a reference to the Governor-General is deemed to include` `anyone else` TRUE)
-- The reference is read as acting with the advice of the Executive Council.
#ASSERT `the reference is read as acting with the advice of the Executive Council` `the Governor-General` FALSE
#ASSERT `the reference is read as acting with the advice of the Executive Council` `the person for the time being administering the Government of the Commonwealth` FALSE
#ASSERT `the reference is read as acting with the advice of the Executive Council` `a person to whom the Governor-General or the administrator has for the time being assigned a power or function as deputy` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the reference is read as acting with the advice of the Executive Council` `anyone else` FALSE)

§ `Section 16B`

#ASSERT `a reference to the Governor of a State is deemed to include` `the Governor for the time being of the State`
#ASSERT `a reference to the Governor of a State is deemed to include` `another person who is for the time being the chief executive officer or administrator of the government of the State`
#ASSERT NOT (`a reference to the Governor of a State is deemed to include` `anyone else`)

§ `Section 16BA`

#ASSERT `a reference to a judge includes` `a Judge or acting Judge of the Local Court of New South Wales` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a reference to a judge includes` `a Judge or acting Judge of the Local Court of the Northern Territory` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Any other judge: the section does not decide; the ordinary meaning of "judge" does.
#ASSERT `a reference to a judge includes` `any other judge` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 16C`

-- (1) and (3): a reference to a Stipendiary Magistrate includes a Magistrate whose office carries an annual salary, and a Local Court Judge.
#ASSERT `a reference to a Stipendiary Magistrate includes` `any other Magistrate` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a reference to a Stipendiary Magistrate includes` `any other Magistrate` FALSE)
#ASSERT `a reference to a Stipendiary Magistrate includes` `a Chief Magistrate` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a reference to a Stipendiary Magistrate includes` `a Chief Magistrate` FALSE)
#ASSERT `a reference to a Stipendiary Magistrate includes` `a Judge or acting Judge of the Local Court of New South Wales` FALSE
#ASSERT `a reference to a Stipendiary Magistrate includes` `a Judge or acting Judge of the Local Court of the Northern Territory` FALSE
-- (2): in an Act passed after the commencement of s 16C, a reference to a Magistrate means a Chief, Police, Stipendiary, Resident or Special Magistrate, or any other Magistrate paid an annual salary.
#ASSERT `a reference to a Magistrate includes` `a Chief Magistrate` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to a Magistrate includes` `a Police Magistrate` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to a Magistrate includes` `a Stipendiary Magistrate` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to a Magistrate includes` `a Resident Magistrate` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to a Magistrate includes` `a Special Magistrate` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to a Magistrate includes` `any other Magistrate` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to a Magistrate includes` `any other Magistrate` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An Act passed before s 16C commenced: (2) says nothing.
#ASSERT `a reference to a Magistrate includes` `a Chief Magistrate` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a reference to a Magistrate includes` `any other Magistrate` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): in any Act, the Local Court Judges are included, whatever the Act's date.
#ASSERT `a reference to a Magistrate includes` `a Judge or acting Judge of the Local Court of New South Wales` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to a Magistrate includes` `a Judge or acting Judge of the Local Court of the Northern Territory` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Section 17A`

#ASSERT `the words are deemed to refer to the Government Printer` `Government Printer of the Commonwealth` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the words are deemed to refer to the Government Printer` `Government Printer of the Commonwealth of Australia` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the words are deemed to refer to the Government Printer` `Commonwealth Government Printer` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the words are deemed to refer to the Government Printer` `Government Printer of Australia` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Other words, or an Act that refers to no such paper: nothing is said.
#ASSERT `the words are deemed to refer to the Government Printer` `other words` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the words are deemed to refer to the Government Printer` `Government Printer of the Commonwealth` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 18A`

#ASSERT `has a corresponding meaning` `another part of speech of that word or phrase` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `has a corresponding meaning` `another grammatical form of that word or phrase` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `has a corresponding meaning` `a different word or phrase` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `has a corresponding meaning` `the word or phrase as it is given its particular meaning` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Where no word or phrase is given a particular meaning, the section does not apply.
#ASSERT `has a corresponding meaning` `another part of speech of that word or phrase` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 18B(4) to (6)`

-- Chosen title.
#ASSERT `the person may be referred to by this deputy chair title` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- No choice: the title the person addressing them considers appropriate.
#ASSERT `the person may be referred to by this deputy chair title` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the person may be referred to by this deputy chair title` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Not an office established by an Act with a deputy chair title.
#ASSERT NOT (`the person may be referred to by this deputy chair title` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- The four deputy chair titles of (4).
#ASSERT `Deputy Chair` EQUALS `Deputy Chair`
#ASSERT NOT (`Deputy Chairwoman` EQUALS `Deputy Chairman`)

§ `Section 20`

#ASSERT `a reference to the holder or occupier includes the person` `holds or occupies it for the time being` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to the holder or occupier includes the person` `performs its duties for the time being` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to the holder or occupier includes the person` `neither holds nor occupies it nor performs its duties` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not a provision of an Act or Commonwealth agreement, or not a reference in general terms: s 20 does not speak.
#ASSERT `a reference to the holder or occupier includes the person` `holds or occupies it for the time being` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a reference to the holder or occupier includes the person` `holds or occupies it for the time being` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 21`

#ASSERT `a reference in an Act to it is construed as` `an officer` EQUALS `a reference to such an officer or office in and for the Commonwealth`
#ASSERT `a reference in an Act to it is construed as` `an office` EQUALS `a reference to such an officer or office in and for the Commonwealth`
#ASSERT `a reference in an Act to it is construed as` `a locality` EQUALS `a reference to such localities, jurisdictions and other matters and things in and of the Commonwealth`
#ASSERT `a reference in an Act to it is construed as` `a jurisdiction` EQUALS `a reference to such localities, jurisdictions and other matters and things in and of the Commonwealth`
#ASSERT `a reference in an Act to it is construed as` `another matter or thing` EQUALS `a reference to such localities, jurisdictions and other matters and things in and of the Commonwealth`

§ `Section 23`

-- (a) words importing a gender include every other gender.
#ASSERT `words importing a gender include` `feminine` `when the word imports` `masculine` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `words importing a gender include` `masculine` `when the word imports` `feminine` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `words importing a gender include` `another gender` `when the word imports` `masculine` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A word that imports no gender: (a) does not speak.
#ASSERT `words importing a gender include` `masculine` `when the word imports` `no gender` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b) the singular includes the plural and the plural the singular.
#ASSERT `words in a number include` `plural` `when the word is in the` `singular`
#ASSERT `words in a number include` `singular` `when the word is in the` `plural`
#ASSERT `words in a number include` `singular` `when the word is in the` `singular`
#ASSERT `words in a number include` `plural` `when the word is in the` `plural`
